; loop-counter-demo.moleasm
;
; Two-register worked example covering both bounded-loop idioms.
;
;   Part 1: send 8 dominant bits via a LOAD_LOOP / DEC / BRANCH_ON
;           triple on R6. Models a write-one-byte that pulls SDA
;           low for each bit's data-valid window.
;
;   Part 2: nested loop --- outer R5 = 3 (rows), inner R6 = 4
;           (columns), MARK each (row, col) so the result ring has a
;           clear timeline. 12 marker records, then HALT.
;
; The wire is just I2C-OD-ish (no real Start/Stop, no ACK slots) ---
; this is a demo of the loop instructions, not of an I2C transaction.
; For a real I2C write-one-byte using the same loop structure, see
; the moleasm book chapter on bounded loops.
;
; -------------------------------------------------------------------------
; v0.2 spelling
; -------------------------------------------------------------------------
;
; v0.2 split the v0 fused `DEC_BRANCH lcrN, label` into the
; hazard-free pair `DEC Rx` + `BRANCH_ON {REG_ZERO|NOT_REG_ZERO},
; label` (§5.19 / §14). The `LOAD_LOOP n` sugar still exists but
; only targets R6 (§5.18). For nested loops the outer counter has
; no sugar --- use raw `LOAD_IMM R5, n` instead, by convention.
;
; EMIT_BIT/EMIT_QUARTER are now suffixed _IMM in v0.2; LOAD_TIMING
; takes positional reg/divider (reg=0 = i2c quarter-bit divider per
; §5.17).

                LOAD_TIMING   reg=0, divider=36   ; ~166 kHz @ 24 MHz Verde
                SET_BUS_MODE  i2c

                ; -- Part 1: send 8 dominant bits via R6 --
                MARK          label=1
                LOAD_LOOP     8
bit_loop:       EMIT_BIT_IMM  tx=dominant
                DEC           R6
                BRANCH_ON     NOT_REG_ZERO, bit_loop
                MARK          label=2

                ; -- Part 2: nested loop, R5 outer / R6 inner --
                LOAD_IMM      R5, 3
row_loop:       MARK          label=3
                LOAD_LOOP     4
col_loop:       MARK          label=4
                DEC           R6
                BRANCH_ON     NOT_REG_ZERO, col_loop
                MARK          label=5
                DEC           R5
                BRANCH_ON     NOT_REG_ZERO, row_loop

                HALT          status=0
